  "slug": "environment-shape-regulatory-variation-1c31",
  "summary": "Long-read, parent-of-origin and pangenome assemblies now show that reference choice alters allele-specific expression and trait interpretation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these preprints is that genotype-linked measurements depend on the genetic and reference framework used to interpret them. In heat-stressed tetraploid potato, long-read RNA-seq resolves haplotype-specific expression, identifying a heat-inducible allele and a nucleus-targeted HSP40 isoform. A parent-of-origin-resolved Granny Smith apple genome shows that matched references reveal sun-exposure and cold-storage responses that other references miss. In Capsicum, a 48-genome super-pangenome reveals structural variation and the genetic basis of carotenoid and capsaicinoid diversity, and a pangenome-guided k-mer GWAS links pungency and aroma terpene traits to Pun1 haplotypes and TPS genes. Switchgrass eQTL and GxE mapping and pearl millet ionomic stability under drought address related questions with less direct reliance on this framework. What is new is the use of haplotype-resolved and pangenome frameworks to resolve allele-specific and reference-dependent variation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
